{
  "$comment": [
    "Ground-truth corpus for the Smart Camera accuracy harness (npm run test:ocr-accuracy).",
    "One entry = one look at one identifier: `truth` is what is physically stamped, `frames`",
    "is what the OCR engine reported on each live tick of that look, in tick order.",
    "confidence is the engine's own line confidence; `glyphs` is optional per-character",
    "confidence, comma separated, in the same compact order Tesseract emits.",
    "Values marked source=production come from the shop's own database dumps.",
    "Real labelled photos (20-30 plates + 20-30 head-tube stamps) are still needed: drop the",
    "file next to this manifest and replace `frames` with { \"file\": \"photo.jpg\" } — the",
    "harness skips those entries until the WASM browser path is wired for them."
